Update crates flagged by RustSec to their newest semver-compatible
releases with `cargo update -p <crate>@<version> --precise <version>`:
  actix-files 0.7.3 -> 0.7.4 (RUSTSEC-2026-0443)
  actix-http 3.19.0 -> 3.21.0 (RUSTSEC-2026-0446, -0448, -0455)
  actix-web 4.18.1 -> 4.19.0 (RUSTSEC-2026-0447)
  crossbeam-epoch 0.9.18 -> 0.9.21 (RUSTSEC-2026-0204)
  h2 0.4.14 -> 0.4.19 (RUSTSEC-2026-0258)
  pulldown-cmark 0.13.4 -> 0.13.6 (RUSTSEC-2026-0414, -0433)
  rand 0.8.5 -> 0.8.8 (RUSTSEC-2026-0097)
  zstd 0.13.3 -> 0.13.5 (RUSTSEC-2026-0391)
  zstd-safe 7.2.4 -> 7.4.1 (RUSTSEC-2026-0395 to -0406)
actix-http 3.21.0 also takes brotli 9.1.1 and brotli-decompressor 6.3.1.
The windows-sys and heck re-selections cargo made alongside are left out.

Not covered, as no semver-compatible release fixes them: crypto-bigint
0.5 (RUSTSEC-2026-0387), h2 0.3 (RUSTSEC-2026-0258) and rsa 0.9
(RUSTSEC-2023-0071). quick-xml 0.26, quinn-proto and quinn-udp are in the
lockfile but not in the qdrant binary's build.

